      {
        "id": 3971570617,
        "type": "DiffNote",
        "body": "**High. The crash this commit fixes is still reachable through `put <item> bagN` and `get <item|all> bagN` run by a mobile.**\n\nLocation: `src/obj/act.item.c` `sort_object_bag()` line 8333 (`get_char_bag(ch, bagnum)`), reached from `do_put()` line 2118 and `do_get()` lines 2605 and 2676. The guard added here covers only `do_sort()`, and the one in `act.informative.c` only `do_bags()`.\n\nDefect: `get_char_bag()` (`src/core/utils.c:11229`) reads `ch->bags->bagN` with no NULL check, and a mobile has `bags == NULL`. `put` and `get` are level-0 commands, so every mobile command path that reaches `sortto` reaches them. `put gem bag1` with no object named `bag1` in reach runs `sort_object_bag(ch, \"gem\", SCMD_SORTTO, 1)`; `get gem bag1` and `get all bag1` run it with `SCMD_SORTFROM`. Each ends the server in a segmentation fault.\n\nRepro (CuTest, the fixture of `Test_gameplay_bag_commands_refuse_a_character_without_bags`, run on `0a662d23a`):\n\n```\ndo_put(&fixture.actor, \"gem bag1\", 0, 0);\n  SIGSEGV get_char_bag utils.c:11229 <- sort_object_bag act.item.c:8333 <- impl_do_put_ act.item.c:2118\ndo_get(&fixture.actor, \"gem bag1\", 0, 0);\n  SIGSEGV get_char_bag utils.c:11229 <- sort_object_bag act.item.c:8333 <- impl_do_get_ act.item.c:2605\ndo_get(&fixture.actor, \"all bag1\", 0, 0);\n  same backtrace\n```\n\nFix: move the `ch->bags == NULL` refusal from `do_sort()` to the top of `sort_object_bag()`, so the three commands share it, and add the `do_put` and two `do_get` calls to the refusal test. The sort-to path needs the guard for more than the crash: `obj_from_char(obj); obj_to_bag(ch, obj, bagnum)` with `bags == NULL` logs a SYSERR and leaves the object in `object_list` held by no one, the leak this MR is about.",
        "author": {
          "id": 42759441,
          "username": "max757",
          "public_email": "",
          "name": "Max aka Mosheh",
          "state": "active",
          "locked": false,
