        "id": 3972143446,
        "type": "DiffNote",
        "body": "Confirmed and fixed in `f14da1d13` as proposed: the refusal moves from `do_sort()` to the top of\n`sort_object_bag()`, so `sortto`, `sortfrom`, `put <item> bagN` and `get <item|all> bagN` share\nit. Every `do_sort()` path that touches a bag ends in `sort_object_bag()` (the `sortto all` path\ngoes through `auto_sort_obj()` and back into `do_sort()`), so `do_sort()` keeps no check of its\nown. The sort-to path is refused before `obj_from_char()`, so nothing is left held by no one.\n\n`Test_gameplay_bag_commands_refuse_a_character_without_bags` runs the three calls from the repro\nafter the sort commands: eight refusals, and the gem is still carried. On `0a662d23a` with the\ntest alone it ends in SIGSEGV at the `do_put()`, with the backtrace in the thread. Clean under\nvalgrind.",
