        "id": 3971570824,
        "type": "DiffNote",
        "body": "**High. `stat file <player who is not online>` ends the server in this loop.**\n\nLocation: `src/core/handler.c` lines 3302-3309. The loop runs for every non-NPC, and `get_char_bag()` (`src/core/utils.c:11229`) dereferences `ch->bags` unconditionally. The comment reads \"only a player has bags\"; what matters is whether `ch->bags` was allocated, and `load_char()` (`src/player/players.c`) never allocates it. Only `init_char()`, `new_char()` and the login path in `interpreter.c:7817` do.\n\nDefect: `do_stat()` (`src/act/act.wizard.c:1730-1743`) builds the body of a player who is not online with `CREATE` + `clear_char()` + `player_specials`, loads it with `load_char()`, puts it in the room and calls `extract_char(victim)`. At the end of the pulse `extract_char_final()` reads `victim->bags->bag1` through NULL. The `empty_bags_to_inventory()` this MR removes read the same pointer, so master has the crash too; this MR rewrites the lines and states the invariant that does not hold.\n\nRepro: as staff, `stat file <name>` for a player who is not logged in: the server dies when the pulse's extractions run. CuTest on `0a662d23a`: a `clear_char()`ed player body with `player_specials` set, placed in a fixture room, then `extract_char_final(&body)`:\n\n```\nSIGSEGV get_char_bag utils.c:11229 <- extract_char_final handler.c:3305\n```\n\nFix: make `get_char_bag()` return NULL when `ch->bags == NULL`. That also covers the loop `objsave_save_and_extract()` gains in this MR. Test it with a player body that has no bag storage.",
        "author": {
          "id": 42759441,
          "username": "max757",
          "public_email": "",
          "name": "Max aka Mosheh",
          "state": "active",
          "locked": false,
          "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/3c7c169343bd7d0f4575137ce8065aee7cb44024d447bbfe66d773133a81c43e?s=80&d=identicon",
