      {
        "id": 3972143811,
        "type": "DiffNote",
        "body": "Confirmed and fixed in `edf0ce122` as proposed: `get_char_bag()` returns NULL when `ch->bags` is\nNULL, which covers the extraction loop and the loop `objsave_save_and_extract()` gained. The\nextraction loop drops its `!IS_NPC(ch)` test, and its comment now says what holds: a character\nwithout bag storage has no bagged objects.\n\n`Test_gameplay_extraction_of_a_player_body_without_bags` builds a body as `stat file` does\n(`CREATE`, `clear_char()`, `player_specials`, `new_mobile_data()`, no bags), puts it in a fixture\nroom and calls `extract_char_final()`: the room's people and contents are as they were. On\n`0a662d23a` with the test alone it ends in SIGSEGV in `get_char_bag()`. Clean under valgrind.\n\nOne correction to the repro's route. Through `stat file` the body never reaches\n`extract_char_final()`: `extract_char()` only flags it and counts a pending extraction, and\n`extract_pending_chars()` walks `character_list`, which the body was never put on (only\n`create_char()`, `read_mobile()` and the login path add to it). So on master `stat file` for a\nplayer who is not online logs `SYSERR: extract_pending_chars() - 1 extraction(s) still pending`\nand leaves the body in room 0's people list, unfreed, rather than dying. That is a pre-existing\n`do_stat()` defect outside this MR, filed as #32 with the fix (`char_from_room()` and\n`free_char()` in place of `extract_char()`). The invariant finding stands regardless: any body\nwithout bag storage that is extracted hit the loop, and now does not.",
        "author": {
          "id": 42759441,
          "username": "max757",
          "public_email": "",
          "name": "Max aka Mosheh",
          "state": "active",
          "locked": false,
