      {
        "id": 3971571003,
        "type": "DiffNote",
        "body": "**Low. The empty save after a drop is tried once and fails silently, leaving the duplication in place.**\n\nLocation: `src/core/handler.c` line 3410.\n\nDefect: `Crash_crashsave()` returns false when `objsave_write_player_save()` cannot start its transaction, delete the rows or commit (connection lost, deadlock, the cases `objsave_save_and_extract()` in this same MR writes a second time for). Nothing reads the result here. The rows of the last save then stay while the objects lie in the room, and the next login restores all of them: the duplication this commit sets out to stop. The sibling path writes a second time and tells the staff through `mudlog()`; this call does neither, and the `log()` inside `objsave_begin_player_save()` is the only trace. The `PLR_CRASH` it sets goes with the character.\n\nRepro: make `objsave_begin_player_save()` fail once (drop the database connection between a staff purge's `extract_char()` and the end of the pulse). The purged character's rows remain; its next login carries what the room holds.\n\nFix: treat it as `objsave_save_and_extract()` does:\n\n```c\nif (dropped && GET_PFILEPOS(ch) >= 0 && !Crash_crashsave(ch) && !Crash_crashsave(ch))\n  mudlog(BRF, LVL_STAFF, TRUE,\n         \"SYSERR: %s's object save could not be emptied as the character left the game; its \"\n         \"next login brings back what it dropped in the room.\",\n         GET_NAME(ch));\n```\n\nor share one retry-and-report helper between the two.",
        "author": {
          "id": 42759441,
          "username": "max757",
          "public_email": "",
          "name": "Max aka Mosheh",
          "state": "active",
          "locked": false,
          "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/3c7c169343bd7d0f4575137ce8065aee7cb44024d447bbfe66d773133a81c43e?s=80&d=identicon",
          "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/max757"
