      {
        "id": 3972144342,
        "type": "DiffNote",
        "body": "Confirmed and fixed in `f6e48f0e9` with the inline form proposed: `Crash_crashsave()` is tried\ntwice, and after two failures the staff hear\n`SYSERR: <name>'s object save could not be emptied as the character left the game; its next login\nbrings back what it dropped in the room.` No shared helper: the two sites write different saves\n(the static rent, idle and cryo writer against the public crash save) and would share four lines.\n`PLR_CRASH` from a failed attempt stays on a character that goes to the menu, where it is what the\nflag is for.\n\n`Test_leaving_without_a_save_writes_the_empty_save_again_and_tells_the_staff`: the connection goes\nas the first attempt deletes the last save's rows (`mysql_test_drop_connection_at()` on the\n`delete from player_save_objs` statement), the second attempt empties the save, and the staff hear\nnothing; then the database is away for both attempts (port 1, socket dropped, as the leaving-save\nretry test does), the one row of the last save stands, and the staff hear the message. On\n`0a662d23a` with the test alone its first half fails with the row still there. Clean under valgrind\nwith the database on.\n\n`docs/systems/SAVE_SYSTEMS_BREAKDOWN.md` says so under \"Leaving without a save\".",
        "author": {
