    "notes": [
      {
        "id": 3971574467,
        "type": null,
        "body": "Adversarial review of `0a662d23a` (tag `object-save-fixes-p4`): three findings, each a thread on the diff.\n\n1. High, `src/obj/act.item.c:8454`: the mobile crash this MR fixes for `sortto`, `sortfrom` and `bags` is still reachable through `put <item> bagN` and `get <item|all> bagN` (`sort_object_bag()` -> `get_char_bag()`). Reproduced, three SIGSEGV backtraces in the thread.\n2. High, `src/core/handler.c:3305`: the new extraction loop dereferences `ch->bags` for every player body, and `stat file <player who is not online>` builds one without it and extracts it, so the server dies. Pre-existing through `empty_bags_to_inventory()`, rewritten here with a comment that states the invariant that does not hold. Reproduced.\n3. Low, `src/core/handler.c:3410`: the empty save after a drop is tried once and its failure is ignored, unlike the retry-and-mudlog in `objsave_save_and_extract()`; on a failed write the duplication this commit stops is back.\n\nChecked and found sound: the rent, idle and cryo paths extract the bags through `extract_obj()` -> `obj_from_bag()` by way of the domain registry (its generation counter starts at 1, so no init-order dependence); player death never reaches `extract_char_final()` (`raw_kill()` keeps the character); the pilot, caster-proxy, follower and vessel extractions are NPC-only; a player in `NOWHERE` exits before the loop; `obj_to_room()` re-reads the bag head each turn, so a reentrant handler cannot skip an object. The three new tests pass alone against a fresh `master_schema.sql` database (`CUTEST_FILTER` per test, seed 1).",
        "author": {
          "id": 42759441,
          "username": "max757",
          "public_email": "",
          "name": "Max aka Mosheh",
          "state": "active",
          "locked": false,
