      {
        "id": 3972145550,
        "type": null,
        "body": "Review of `0a662d23a` (tag `object-save-fixes-p4`) addressed: all three findings confirmed and\nfixed, each thread answered and resolved. The tag stays on the branch; no rebase or squash, and\nthe branch is still on `master`'s tip (`529fee05d`).\n\n| Thread | Fix |\n| -- | -- |\n| `put`/`get` into a bag by a mobile (high) | `f14da1d13`: the refusal moves into `sort_object_bag()` |\n| `get_char_bag()` on a body without bag storage (high) | `edf0ce122`: it answers NULL |\n| Empty save tried once (low) | `f6e48f0e9`: tried twice, then `mudlog()` |\n\n`074fd1e89` records the review in the plan. Found on the way: through `stat file` the body never\nreaches `extract_char_final()` (it is not on `character_list`), so on master it is left in room 0\nunfreed rather than crashing; that is work item #32, outside this MR.\n\nVerification on `f6e48f0e9`:\n\n- Each new test fails on `0a662d23a`: SIGSEGV in `get_char_bag()` for the two bag tests, the\n  last save's row still there for the retry test.\n- The five bag and leaving tests are clean under valgrind, the three leaving tests with the\n  database on.\n- `make -j16 test`: 2053 tests pass. `make install` done.\n- `./cutest` with the database tests on, on a database freshly built from `sql/master_schema.sql`:\n  2053 of 2053 pass.\n- `python3 scripts/ci/local/run.py --base gitlab/master`: 33 of 33 jobs pass (552 s); the unit, sanitizer and memory-check jobs run 2053 tests each, and the persistence changed lines are 100% covered.\n- The format, hygiene and secrets jobs pass again on `074fd1e89`, which adds the plan's record\n  only.\n\nReady to merge: merge commit, `squash=false`, `sha=074fd1e89`.",
